            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "The U.S. tax system operates on a principle called \"voluntary compliance.\" This does not mean paying taxes is optional. It means the system relies on individuals to accurately report their income and calculate their tax liability, rather than the government calculating it for you. The Internal Revenue Service (IRS) is the federal agency responsible for administering the tax code and enforcing compliance."
